WEBVTT

00:00:16.840 --> 00:00:18.790
I swear to God it's true!

00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:25.120
You can hear the ball bouncing in the third string gym after practice even though nobody's there!

00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:28.170
Huh?

00:00:29.920 --> 00:00:31.000
That's retarded.

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:32.010
Hey, Dai—

00:00:32.490 --> 00:00:33.910
I mean, Aomine!

00:00:33.910 --> 00:00:37.470
Christ, who's heard of a ghost that shoots hoops?

00:00:38.060 --> 00:00:41.010
Hell, I'll play it one-on-one if that's a fact.

00:00:47.770 --> 00:00:48.900
Hey!

00:00:53.710 --> 00:00:55.210
<i>What the?</i>

00:00:55.210 --> 00:00:56.570
<i>Is this real?</i>

00:00:56.570 --> 00:00:58.830
<i>Was a ghost really playing basketball?!</i>

00:00:58.830 --> 00:01:02.330
<i>No, it must've been someone who just finished practicing...</i>

00:01:02.330 --> 00:01:06.220
<i>But I heard a ball bounce just as I opened the door...</i>

00:01:06.220 --> 00:01:07.080
Excuse me.

00:01:08.670 --> 00:01:10.600
Oh God! Oh God! I won't do it again!

00:01:10.600 --> 00:01:12.260
I won't bring gravure mags to school!

00:01:12.260 --> 00:01:14.590
I won't sleep in class! Away with you, demon!

00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:14.590
Oh?

00:01:14.590 --> 00:01:16.930
It's real! It's real!

00:01:15.730 --> 00:01:16.930
Aomine?

00:01:20.510 --> 00:01:22.410
<i>The first time we met,</i>

00:01:22.410 --> 00:01:27.150
<i>was during the first fall after we enrolled at Teiko Middle School.</i>

00:03:00.130 --> 00:03:03.960
So you're so unnoticeable that nobody knew you were in here?

00:03:03.960 --> 00:03:05.120
Oh man!

00:03:06.430 --> 00:03:08.830
Aomine, you're laughing too much.

00:03:08.830 --> 00:03:09.910
Sorry.

00:03:09.910 --> 00:03:12.080
Wait. You know my name?

00:03:12.760 --> 00:03:16.450
Everybody does since you became a starter as a first year.

00:03:16.450 --> 00:03:18.300
Oh yeah?

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:19.840
And what about you?

00:03:21.370 --> 00:03:22.690
I'm on the third string.

00:03:22.690 --> 00:03:25.530
Not that! I'm asking your name.

00:03:25.530 --> 00:03:28.850
Besides, who cares what string you are?

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:32.730
You love basketball enough to stay every night to practice.

00:03:33.380 --> 00:03:36.330
Any guy who loves basketball is never bad.

00:03:36.330 --> 00:03:37.650
That's what I always say.

00:03:39.510 --> 00:03:40.610
That's a strange saying.

00:03:40.950 --> 00:03:42.010
What?!

00:03:42.010 --> 00:03:44.470
I'm Kuroko Tetsuya. Glad to meet you.

00:03:49.790 --> 00:03:52.370
Are you sure you want to play me?

00:03:52.830 --> 00:03:55.390
Sure, whenever you're ready.

00:03:55.390 --> 00:03:56.340
Is that so?

00:03:59.380 --> 00:04:00.630
Prepare for the worst.

00:04:01.300 --> 00:04:02.260
Right.

00:04:22.770 --> 00:04:24.030
That hurt.

00:04:24.030 --> 00:04:25.160
What the crap?!

00:04:25.820 --> 00:04:29.370
I was expecting something huge when you told me to prepare myself.

00:04:29.370 --> 00:04:32.390
What are you saying? I'm on the third string.

00:04:32.390 --> 00:04:33.620
Huh?

00:04:33.620 --> 00:04:37.490
I told you to literally prepare for the worst, since I'm inexperienced.

00:04:37.490 --> 00:04:39.590
Dude, you're bizarre.

00:04:40.440 --> 00:04:43.050
So... should we stop?

00:05:28.440 --> 00:05:29.450
So, did you just...

00:05:29.450 --> 00:05:30.590
That was great!

00:05:32.150 --> 00:05:34.520
Aomine, can we play another round?

00:05:36.850 --> 00:05:37.640
Sure!

00:05:45.890 --> 00:05:49.640
Okay, I have to return the keys to the staff office now.

00:05:50.430 --> 00:05:51.690
Good night.

00:05:51.690 --> 00:05:52.950
Right, later!

00:05:59.830 --> 00:06:01.670
What a weirdo.

00:06:03.980 --> 00:06:05.090
Thank you very much!

00:06:13.600 --> 00:06:14.850
Oh, thank—

00:06:16.370 --> 00:06:18.780
Hi. We meet again.

00:06:18.780 --> 00:06:20.310
So why are you here?

00:06:21.610 --> 00:06:23.360
Because I like...{fujos say kyaah}

00:06:23.360 --> 00:06:24.810
the vanilla shake here.

00:06:27.150 --> 00:06:28.400
Huh?

00:06:29.270 --> 00:06:30.430
Here.

00:06:32.730 --> 00:06:34.780
That ain't gonna be enough for you.

00:06:34.780 --> 00:06:35.830
You can have one.

00:06:37.550 --> 00:06:38.790
Thank you very much.

00:06:40.610 --> 00:06:42.220
You live this way?

00:06:42.220 --> 00:06:42.900
Yes.

00:06:42.900 --> 00:06:44.750
Then let's walk together.

00:06:44.750 --> 00:06:45.580
Of course.

00:06:46.310 --> 00:06:47.140
But...

00:06:48.220 --> 00:06:52.250
I don't think it's right to walk with my hands full.

00:06:52.250 --> 00:06:55.170
Are you... going to be a problem?

00:06:57.090 --> 00:06:58.100
I see...

00:06:58.100 --> 00:07:02.000
So you stay back practicing late so you can move up?

00:07:02.000 --> 00:07:02.790
Yes.

00:07:02.790 --> 00:07:04.650
I want to improve as much as I can.

00:07:05.060 --> 00:07:06.500
That's awesome.

00:07:06.500 --> 00:07:09.760
Even most first stringers aren't that dedicated.

00:07:09.760 --> 00:07:12.030
But I still have a long way to go.

00:07:12.970 --> 00:07:16.240
I now know after seeing you play

00:07:16.240 --> 00:07:19.080
that I may never make it to the first string.

00:07:21.210 --> 00:07:22.370
Yeah look,

00:07:22.370 --> 00:07:26.500
why weren't you faked out when I first had the ball in our one-on-one?

00:07:27.480 --> 00:07:31.800
I thought I put on a really nice juke back there.

00:07:31.800 --> 00:07:35.310
I thought you were going for a fake.

00:07:36.690 --> 00:07:38.140
It was just a hunch.

00:07:39.290 --> 00:07:40.790
But I happened to luck out.

00:07:41.390 --> 00:07:43.070
Oh?

00:07:43.070 --> 00:07:44.760
<i>That wasn't luck.</i>

00:07:44.760 --> 00:07:47.360
<i>He anticipated all my moves.</i>

00:07:47.890 --> 00:07:50.890
<i>Though it didn't matter since he's slow.</i>

00:07:51.930 --> 00:07:54.140
<i>But, boring he's not.</i>

00:08:03.740 --> 00:08:05.220
Oh, Tetsu!

00:08:06.450 --> 00:08:08.710
You wanna head to practice together?

00:08:10.600 --> 00:08:11.170
But—

00:08:11.170 --> 00:08:13.520
You don't have to do that crap!

00:08:15.030 --> 00:08:17.690
Aomine. We are not done cleaning.

00:08:15.030 --> 00:08:15.960
Hey!

00:08:17.690 --> 00:08:19.060
Y-You!

00:08:19.060 --> 00:08:20.610
Midorima, what the hell is this?!

00:08:20.610 --> 00:08:22.560
It is today's lucky item.

00:08:22.560 --> 00:08:23.600
O-Ow!

00:08:23.600 --> 00:08:24.650
That's not what I meant!

00:08:24.650 --> 00:08:27.020
<i>Aomine and I were different in so many ways,</i>

00:08:27.470 --> 00:08:30.870
<i>I honestly did not think we could bond.</i>

00:08:31.930 --> 00:08:35.450
<i>However, I easily looked past those differences,</i>

00:08:37.070 --> 00:08:40.990
<i>because I was completely awed and inspired by his skills.</i>

00:08:50.150 --> 00:08:51.410
Something wrong?

00:08:51.410 --> 00:08:52.630
No.

00:08:52.630 --> 00:08:54.550
I think you're amazing.

00:08:57.740 --> 00:09:03.810
If that's what you're getting at,
I think you're the one who's amazing.

00:09:04.450 --> 00:09:07.670
There aren't many dudes who love basketball more than me.

00:09:11.230 --> 00:09:15.030
We'll hit the court together one of these days, Tetsu.

00:09:16.850 --> 00:09:17.410
Of course.

00:09:23.500 --> 00:09:27.790
I went to cheer for them that game, and it was awesome!

00:09:28.160 --> 00:09:34.440
Especially when the first year Aomine went at it with Kamizaki's second year Inoue!

00:09:34.440 --> 00:09:37.250
Neither of them gave an inch. It was so intense!

00:09:37.250 --> 00:09:38.490
Wow.

00:09:46.170 --> 00:09:46.980
Huh?

00:09:46.980 --> 00:09:48.650
Upper string tryouts are today?

00:09:48.650 --> 00:09:49.630
Yes.

00:09:49.630 --> 00:09:52.110
They should be looking at the second and third strings.

00:09:52.910 --> 00:09:55.070
Some will make it to the first string.

00:09:55.070 --> 00:09:56.380
I see.

00:09:57.480 --> 00:09:58.030
All right!

00:10:00.070 --> 00:10:02.740
Ah, Mine-chin, are you still practicing?

00:10:02.740 --> 00:10:03.500
Yeah!

00:10:03.500 --> 00:10:06.790
I'm gonna get 20 points off Inoue next time we meet!

00:10:07.250 --> 00:10:09.730
Oh? Good luck with that.

00:10:09.730 --> 00:10:12.750
Hey, what are you doing, Mido-chin?

00:10:13.110 --> 00:10:15.680
There has been a strange odor recently.

00:10:15.680 --> 00:10:17.470
Oh, that.

00:10:18.750 --> 00:10:20.220
Mine-chin and {Hai}Zaki-chin

00:10:20.910 --> 00:10:24.370
have been stuffing their lockers with dirty t-shirts.

00:10:24.370 --> 00:10:25.180
What—

00:10:25.720 --> 00:10:28.190
Aomine!

00:10:40.100 --> 00:10:40.930
Oh!

00:10:40.930 --> 00:10:41.700
You're late!

00:10:42.430 --> 00:10:43.390
I thought...

00:10:46.360 --> 00:10:47.230
What's wrong?

00:10:48.490 --> 00:10:49.460
Aomine.

00:10:50.370 --> 00:10:51.880
Something wrong with you?

00:10:53.820 --> 00:10:55.420
I think...

00:10:57.170 --> 00:10:58.800
I should quit the team.

00:11:00.290 --> 00:11:02.770
Huh? Why?

00:11:02.770 --> 00:11:05.070
With my lack of skills,

00:11:05.070 --> 00:11:07.570
I won't get to play with you.

00:11:08.190 --> 00:11:10.650
I can't even make the second string.

00:11:11.700 --> 00:11:13.240
I love basketball.

00:11:13.240 --> 00:11:16.330
But it's been six months now.

00:11:16.330 --> 00:11:19.490
It's obvious that I'm not cut out for it.

00:11:20.830 --> 00:11:23.110
There's no way I can possibly

00:11:23.720 --> 00:11:27.290
contribute to a basketball team like Teiko.

00:11:28.130 --> 00:11:31.230
There's no such thing as a useless player.

00:11:32.170 --> 00:11:34.390
Even if you don't get to play,

00:11:34.390 --> 00:11:40.430
you stay back and literally practice longer than anyone, including the first stringers!

00:11:40.430 --> 00:11:43.220
I refuse to accept there's no hope for you!

00:11:43.810 --> 00:11:47.270
I have so much respect for you.

00:11:47.270 --> 00:11:49.180
You make me want to work harder!

00:11:49.930 --> 00:11:53.210
I'm not saying you'll definitely make it if you don't quit.

00:11:53.210 --> 00:11:55.400
But if you quit, you'll never know!

00:11:56.680 --> 00:11:57.610
I...

00:11:59.160 --> 00:12:01.110
I don't want you to quit!

00:12:07.510 --> 00:12:08.540
Aomine.

00:12:10.650 --> 00:12:13.080
Is this where you were practicing?

00:12:13.080 --> 00:12:13.500
Yeah.

00:12:14.170 --> 00:12:16.460
There are too many people in the other gym.

00:12:16.460 --> 00:12:18.390
Wow, you practice all alone?

00:12:18.390 --> 00:12:19.980
Not quite.

00:12:22.160 --> 00:12:25.140
W-Whoa, really?

00:12:25.140 --> 00:12:27.010
When did he...?

00:12:27.010 --> 00:12:27.820
Who is he?

00:12:27.820 --> 00:12:28.830
Tetsu.

00:12:28.830 --> 00:12:31.100
We always practice together.

00:12:31.100 --> 00:12:33.300
And he's on our team?

00:12:33.300 --> 00:12:35.040
He's not a first stringer though.

00:12:35.040 --> 00:12:36.560
He's still third string.

00:12:36.560 --> 00:12:38.920
Oh, no wonder.

00:12:39.610 --> 00:12:41.710
Let's go already.

00:12:41.710 --> 00:12:42.910
No.

00:12:42.910 --> 00:12:44.530
There's something about him.

00:12:47.370 --> 00:12:50.490
You're fascinating. I've never seen anybody like you.

00:12:53.850 --> 00:12:59.110
You may even have a secret talent completely dissimilar to ours.

00:13:21.840 --> 00:13:24.900
Man... we're scoring points like crazy.

00:13:25.910 --> 00:13:27.870
Especially those two.

00:13:28.730 --> 00:13:30.910
Did you know it would turn out this way?

00:13:30.910 --> 00:13:32.330
He surpassed even my expectations.

00:13:38.940 --> 00:13:39.790
Tetsu!

00:13:48.770 --> 00:13:51.350
<i>The first time we stood on the court together</i>

00:13:51.350 --> 00:13:53.430
<i>was at the end of winter.</i>

00:14:02.580 --> 00:14:07.070
Aomine's ruthless. He scored 80 points on them.

00:14:07.700 --> 00:14:11.030
This isn't even a game with Aomine around.

00:14:11.440 --> 00:14:14.280
The guy's not simply gifted. He's a freak.

00:14:17.550 --> 00:14:21.960
<i>By summer, Aomine began skipping practice.</i>

00:14:27.470 --> 00:14:29.890
Aominecchi's not here today?

00:14:29.890 --> 00:14:32.410
Yes, and neither is Kuroko.

00:14:32.410 --> 00:14:33.550
Kurokocchi?

00:14:34.850 --> 00:14:36.930
That's pretty surprising.

00:14:36.930 --> 00:14:39.940
He probably felt he had to do something.

00:14:40.810 --> 00:14:44.910
But there's likely nothing he can say to solve <i>that</i> problem.

00:14:53.520 --> 00:14:54.570
Aomine!

00:14:55.990 --> 00:14:57.260
Tetsu...

00:14:57.260 --> 00:14:58.610
What about practice?

00:14:59.390 --> 00:15:00.710
Can we walk home together?

00:15:03.190 --> 00:15:05.170
Sure, let's do that.

00:15:07.070 --> 00:15:08.390
Aomine,

00:15:08.390 --> 00:15:11.250
you've started skipping practice more lately.

00:15:11.250 --> 00:15:12.370
Yeah...

00:15:14.250 --> 00:15:15.620
It's cool though.

00:15:15.620 --> 00:15:18.240
If I practice, I'll just get even better.

00:15:18.240 --> 00:15:22.190
The harder I try, the more boring basketball gets.

00:15:23.110 --> 00:15:24.650
And besides...

00:15:25.810 --> 00:15:27.950
What I really want is never...

00:15:29.590 --> 00:15:33.570
Basketball's just a game anyway.

00:15:34.310 --> 00:15:37.200
I'm going to start skipping games too.

00:15:39.240 --> 00:15:40.500
You can't do that.

00:15:41.640 --> 00:15:42.960
A popsicle?

00:15:44.010 --> 00:15:48.000
It takes everything I have to keep up with everyone else,

00:15:48.000 --> 00:15:50.920
so I don't know how you feel.

00:15:51.720 --> 00:15:54.560
But no matter how large the difference in our skill,

00:15:54.560 --> 00:15:56.890
I'd never want you to hold back or ease up on me

00:15:57.630 --> 00:16:00.350
if I were your opponent!

00:16:03.020 --> 00:16:07.970
Besides, I'm sure you'll meet someone more amazing than yourself soon.

00:16:14.090 --> 00:16:15.780
You're right.

00:16:15.780 --> 00:16:16.810
That's right.

00:16:21.820 --> 00:16:26.820
Oh yeah, I still haven't gotten 20 points off Kamizaki's Inoue.

00:16:26.820 --> 00:16:29.720
The dude's probably gotten even better.

00:16:30.530 --> 00:16:34.870
Yet you say you'll skip games while he's still out there?

00:16:34.870 --> 00:16:36.190
Cram it!

00:16:36.190 --> 00:16:36.870
Noogie, noogie!

00:16:36.870 --> 00:16:37.890
That hurts!

00:17:00.570 --> 00:17:02.980
We're substituting Kuroko for Kise.

00:17:02.980 --> 00:17:04.460
Other than that, nothing changes.

00:17:05.340 --> 00:17:06.470
We win!

00:17:07.420 --> 00:17:07.960
Yeah!

00:17:14.060 --> 00:17:16.380
Aominecchi, we're about to play.

00:17:16.380 --> 00:17:17.030
Huh?

00:17:17.650 --> 00:17:18.990
Right.

00:17:18.990 --> 00:17:20.810
Eh? What about you?

00:17:20.810 --> 00:17:23.390
Kurokocchi's gone in for me.

00:17:23.390 --> 00:17:25.020
Were you not listening again?

00:17:25.020 --> 00:17:27.050
Sorry, my fault.

00:17:30.940 --> 00:17:32.400
Momoi.

00:17:32.400 --> 00:17:34.290
How many points has Aomine scored so far?

00:17:35.160 --> 00:17:36.860
Thirty-six.

00:17:37.670 --> 00:17:38.810
Is that so?

00:17:40.880 --> 00:17:41.820
Kuroko.

00:17:42.750 --> 00:17:44.930
Keep passing to Aomine.

00:17:44.930 --> 00:17:45.740
Okay.

00:17:46.660 --> 00:17:49.210
We'll show them what a real defeat is like.

00:18:05.690 --> 00:18:07.310
Talk about a one-sided game.

00:18:20.780 --> 00:18:21.620
Got it!

00:18:28.850 --> 00:18:30.660
You don't even need the other four.

00:18:36.170 --> 00:18:37.850
<i>What the hell?</i>

00:18:38.650 --> 00:18:41.690
<i>Have they given up already?</i>

00:18:43.130 --> 00:18:45.750
<i>Is this what happens when I try even a little?</i>

00:18:55.680 --> 00:19:01.240
<i>If my opponents lose the will to play, what's fun about basketball anymore?</i>

00:19:09.350 --> 00:19:10.580
Tetsu.

00:19:12.350 --> 00:19:14.650
Sorry, I just can't.

00:19:20.810 --> 00:19:24.150
The only one who can beat me is me.

00:19:41.340 --> 00:19:44.930
You shot down yet another high-school recruiter?

00:19:44.930 --> 00:19:45.910
What now?

00:19:46.210 --> 00:19:49.370
This makes it how many? Why do you keep rejecting them?

00:19:49.370 --> 00:19:51.660
Who says I rejected them?

00:19:51.660 --> 00:19:57.880
When I tell them I'll play games but skip practice, they say no dice.

00:19:57.880 --> 00:20:02.800
Of course they would! How can you work with your teammates if you don't practice?

00:20:04.510 --> 00:20:05.900
Can it!

00:20:08.130 --> 00:20:13.140
What if practicing makes me eclipse them even more?

00:20:14.320 --> 00:20:15.940
I see...

00:20:15.940 --> 00:20:18.400
That might be a problem.

00:20:21.210 --> 00:20:23.110
But I hear you.

00:20:25.580 --> 00:20:27.690
I'll take your wishes into consideration.

00:20:30.620 --> 00:20:32.590
Oh, there he is!

00:20:34.010 --> 00:20:36.170
Aomine, right?

00:20:36.870 --> 00:20:38.630
Who wants to know?

00:20:38.630 --> 00:20:41.210
Name's Imayoshi Shoichi. It's a pleasure.

00:20:42.090 --> 00:20:46.160
I'm Touou's captain, the same school that just came to recruit you.

00:20:46.160 --> 00:20:47.490
Oh?

00:20:47.490 --> 00:20:48.220
What do you want?

00:20:49.000 --> 00:20:52.210
We've been awfully busy recruiting talent.

00:20:52.210 --> 00:20:55.390
Especially you so-called Generation of Miracles.

00:20:55.390 --> 00:20:58.670
Our school's chomping at the bit to get you fellas.

00:20:58.670 --> 00:21:01.650
So I wanted to have a little look-see myself.

00:21:01.650 --> 00:21:03.050
Oh yeah?

00:21:03.050 --> 00:21:05.610
Find out anything?

00:21:05.610 --> 00:21:07.680
Yeah, let's see...

00:21:07.680 --> 00:21:10.130
Just like I thought... but not really.

00:21:10.130 --> 00:21:11.580
You're actually

00:21:12.610 --> 00:21:15.240
softer than I might've imagined.

00:21:15.240 --> 00:21:18.000
It's best if you don't come to our school.

00:21:18.000 --> 00:21:19.250
What?

00:21:19.720 --> 00:21:23.270
I had a glance at your most recent game footage.

00:21:23.270 --> 00:21:26.170
Though you knew you're gonna win,

00:21:26.170 --> 00:21:29.440
your play told me a part of you wants to lose.

00:21:30.430 --> 00:21:34.980
All that power went and made you sad and lonely.

00:21:34.980 --> 00:21:38.720
You couldn't bear it, so you've been waiting, right?

00:21:38.720 --> 00:21:42.880
Waiting for a guy who's just as good, or even better than you.

00:21:43.360 --> 00:21:48.730
But... I'm afraid nobody in their right mind wants that in a player.

00:21:50.530 --> 00:21:52.630
And that goes double for us.

00:21:52.630 --> 00:21:55.990
That's why our coach is tabling his decision.

00:21:56.980 --> 00:21:58.000
Anyway...

00:21:58.440 --> 00:21:59.960
Once you're done waiting

00:22:01.790 --> 00:22:06.470
and are ready to be the best, we'll gladly take you.

00:22:08.990 --> 00:22:10.430
You're a funny guy.

00:22:12.050 --> 00:22:13.650
I'll think about it.

00:22:19.410 --> 00:22:21.820
Do you think you can work with him?

00:22:22.320 --> 00:22:24.740
As long as I give him a long leash.

00:22:24.740 --> 00:22:28.950
I have my reservations, but I'll still bet the farm on his skills.

00:22:28.590 --> 00:22:35.300
{2nd ED Season 2}

00:23:41.220 --> 00:23:44.180
<i>We would face each other in different uniforms</i>

00:23:44.180 --> 00:23:46.270
<i>just a few months later.</i>
